WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:26.070
&gt;&gt; Hi, this is Andrew and
Michael from Cognition Team.

00:00:26.071 --> 00:00:28.350
This is a demo of the prototype

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:30.185
of Project Kinect for Azure,

00:00:30.186 --> 00:00:32.475
and this is a
time-of-flight sensor

00:00:32.476 --> 00:00:33.750
which going to be used in

00:00:33.751 --> 00:00:35.485
a Project Kinect for Azure as

00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:37.830
well as of the HoloLens
next generation.

00:00:37.831 --> 00:00:40.800
So, what you're seeing right now

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:45.675
is sensor module in our task
case, task prototype case,

00:00:45.676 --> 00:00:47.420
and it's connect to a PC,

00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:50.780
and the PC will do
a local processing to convert

00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:52.730
the raw image to the depth image

00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:55.215
and there render it
into a 3D Point Cloud.

00:00:55.216 --> 00:00:57.710
So, Michael is basically

00:00:57.711 --> 00:00:59.845
the object right now
before the depth camera.

00:00:59.846 --> 00:01:03.595
You can see the details of
his shirt is very clear,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.825
and the stability of
deploying cards very good.

00:01:06.826 --> 00:01:09.910
This camera has
a much better quality.

00:01:09.911 --> 00:01:11.840
There are lots of increments
on the hardware and

00:01:11.841 --> 00:01:13.480
software side, and you can see,

00:01:13.481 --> 00:01:15.260
you can reach to
really close range as

00:01:15.261 --> 00:01:17.395
well if you put your finger
near the camera,

00:01:17.396 --> 00:01:19.630
and he's too got
a very good depth map.

00:01:19.631 --> 00:01:22.190
Then, it has a very
wide field of view,

00:01:22.191 --> 00:01:24.475
you can see I'm also in
the picture as well.

00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:26.475
You may notice that
the range here,

00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:29.050
I'm disappear because
this is a example mode,

00:01:29.051 --> 00:01:30.765
which only showing
the short range.

00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:33.380
But, we can switch to
a long-range as well,

00:01:33.381 --> 00:01:35.270
and you can see is actually
is supporting much

00:01:35.271 --> 00:01:37.510
further and also the Point Cloud

00:01:37.511 --> 00:01:39.115
is really, really stable.

00:01:39.116 --> 00:01:43.145
We are basically targeting
a high accurate depth camera

00:01:43.146 --> 00:01:44.420
with low noise,

00:01:44.421 --> 00:01:46.145
and also this is

00:01:46.146 --> 00:01:49.730
very low power consumption
camera as well.

00:01:49.731 --> 00:01:51.860
Eventually, this will be

00:01:51.861 --> 00:01:54.460
our technology we are
going to use in HoloLens,

00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:56.400
which is trying to help

00:01:56.401 --> 00:02:00.540
people talking in the scenario
like 3D reconstruction,

00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:02.620
or people tracking, and

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:05.150
also hand tracking gesture,
things like that.

00:02:05.151 --> 00:02:07.820
Okay. That is about
this demo and if

00:02:07.821 --> 00:02:10.380
your interesting
Project Kinect Azure,

00:02:10.381 --> 00:02:13.700
please look for Project Kinect
for Azure keyword online.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.805
We have a website that
have all the information,

00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:16.990
you probably can viewing

00:02:16.991 --> 00:02:18.735
a survey and bring your feedback,

00:02:18.736 --> 00:02:20.280
and then keeping tune,

00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:23.200
like we will be there. Thanks.

